From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gdiplus: NN half pixel centre on the image edge (3509)

gdiplus: nearest-neighbour DrawImage with the half pixel offset, centres on the image edge

2653 compares each destination pixel's centre with the image edge. The centre is accumulated step by step
and on 32 bit x86 a centre exactly on the right edge came out just inside it, so test_DrawImage_scale cases
20 and 27 (2.5 times, Half and HighQuality) drew an extra column; stock wine passes them. The comparison
now allows 1e-4 of rounding.
---
--- a/dlls/gdiplus/graphics.c
+++ b/dlls/gdiplus/graphics.c
@@ -3649,15 +3649,18 @@
                     for (x = dst_area.left, src_pointf = src_pointf_row; x < dst_area.right;
                          x++, src_pointf.X += x_dx, src_pointf.Y += x_dy)
                     {
-                        REAL cx = src_pointf.X, cy = src_pointf.Y;
+                        REAL cx = src_pointf.X, cy = src_pointf.Y, eps = 0.0f;
                         if (interpolation == InterpolationModeNearestNeighbor &&
                             (offset_mode == PixelOffsetModeHalf || offset_mode == PixelOffsetModeHighQuality))
                         {
                             cx += 0.5f * (x_dx + y_dx);
                             cy += 0.5f * (x_dy + y_dy);
+                            /* the centre is accumulated step by step: a centre that falls on the edge
+                             * must not land on the wrong side of it by rounding (32 bit x86) */
+                            eps = 1e-4f;
                         }
-                        if (cx >= srcx && cx < srcx + srcwidth &&
-                            cy >= srcy && cy < srcy + srcheight)
+                        if (cx >= srcx - eps && cx < srcx + srcwidth - eps &&
+                            cy >= srcy - eps && cy < srcy + srcheight - eps)
                             *dst_color = resample_bitmap_pixel_footprint(&src_area, src_data, bitmap->width,
                                                                          bitmap->height, &src_pointf, footprint,
                                                                          imageAttributes, interpolation, offset_mode);
